  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The operator journey",
      "items": [
        "The UI posts to /api/panel; the backend slices the fixture once so every system scores identical items in identical order",
        "POST /api/route classifies one text against an arbitrary label set, capped at 512 labels",
        "POST /api/schema-swap hands the model one app's half of a disjoint split, seeded so it reproduces"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One engine, loaded once",
      "items": [
        "The checkpoint loads lazily on first inference, so /api/health answers while ~1.9 GB is still being read",
        "CUDA fp16 on Turing; the CPU fallback is ~9x slower at 77 labels, and the UI says so instead of pretending",
        "Attention is not forced: the checkpoint config decides, and /api/health reports what transformers resolved rather than a policy nobody applied"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Honest arms",
      "items": [
        "A system that cannot run lands in unavailable with a reason; it is never dropped and never invents a number",
        "A null cost is not $0.00 — the panel says free, priced or unpriced, because those are three different claims",
        "The majority-class floor row is always kept, and macro-F1 is reported next to accuracy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Offline setup and the gates",
      "items": [
        "fetch_model.py resumes the checkpoint download; fetch_fixtures.py --with-train writes the two train splits",
        "Only banking77 and clinc150 ship a train split, so the supervised arms report unavailable elsewhere",
        "87 offline tests need no GPU, weights or network; the CUDA and model-card gates stay local and are never promoted into CI"
      ]
    }
  ]
